    "body": "Part 1 of 2 (the ring and the row guide planners) is on the branch `issue/4176-kernel-guides-rings-rows`, head `9dada0b6d`. No PR is open yet: the work builds on K1 (#4025, branch `issue/4025-kernel-region`), and K1 is not merged into `side/path-kernel`. When K1 merges, the branch takes `git merge origin/side/path-kernel` and the draft PR opens with `--base side/path-kernel`.\n\nWhat the branch adds:\n- `RingPlanner`: rings as level sets of the distance to the walls (Held 1991), spaced by the stepover of the choice. Clean-up rings fill what the regular rings leave. The 0.1 mm2 guard names each gap.\n- A `FullWidth` mark names each stretch where the tool disc overlaps no deeper ring and no air (#3788). On the waist pin, the middle of each neck strand is named.\n- `RowPlanner`: rows at the angle, clipped to the centre area, with a closing ring on request.\n- `Guides`: sends rings and rows to their planners. It refuses the medial line and the trace by name until part 2.\n\nPins: `laws` suite (`guide_rings`, `guide_rows`) and `pass_start_levels/kernel_rings.rs` (the kernel rings against the old goldens; each difference is named in `docs/decisions/4176-kernel-guides-rings-rows.md`).\n\nGates on the final head, base `origin/issue/4025-kernel-region`: quick gate green, `example_catalog*` green, light lane green, clippy on pathkernel and motion clean. The issue keeps `claimed`: part 2 follows.",
